# Each sum enters the outer loop as the integer 0 and comes round a number. A walk of an inner loop that does not fit, inside a walk of the outer loop that is undone anyway, is left as walked,
# so one walk of the outer loop learns all twelve. It used to end at the first loop that did not fit: a walk of the outer loop for each sum, and behind eleven of them the row claimed nothing:
# every parameter of the outer head was `anything`.
